    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Tanzania was created on 26 April 1964 by the union of mainland Tanganyika and the islands of Zanzibar.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#julius-nyerere">Julius Nyerere</a>’s Arusha Declaration of 1967 made it <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#africa">Africa</a>’s best-known experiment in socialism, known as ujamaa.</li><li>It has had no successful coup or civil war, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#swahili">Swahili</a> gives it one of the strongest national identities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#africa">Africa</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#julius-nyerere">Julius Nyerere</a> translated Shakespeare’s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> and The Merchant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#venice">Venice</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#swahili">Swahili</a>, part of his effort to make Swahili a language of national culture.</p></aside>
    </section>

